      "title": [
       {
        "type": "heading6",
        "text": "Notes for React developers",
        "spans": []
       }
      ],
      "body_text": [
       {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "- The Aalto React libraries are primarily built on a stack that includes React and TypeScript, with minimal additional dependencies. This deliberate choice offers the flexibility to seamlessly integrate our libraries with various React frameworks, like Vite or NextJS. While using TypeScript in the client channel is not mandatory, it is strongly recommended for an optimised development workflow.",
        "spans": [],
        "direction": "ltr"
       },
       {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "- The components are intentionally designed not to manage their own state. This design allows you to integrate these components with a wide range of state management mechanisms.",
        "spans": [],
        "direction": "ltr"
       },
       {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "- By default, the libraries generate plain HTML links for navigation. However, the architecture is built to support more advanced routing solutions. You have the freedom to inject your preferred router, such as React Router, by wrapping your application in the appropriate routing provider.",
        "spans": [],
        "direction": "ltr"
       }
      ],
      "caption": [],
      "cta_label": [],
      "cta_link": {
       "link_type": "Any"
      },
      "cta_link_custom_icon": null,
      "image_aspect_ratio": "hd",
      "content_box_special_icon": null,
      "video": {
       "link_type": "Any"
      }
     }
    ],
    "id": "content_tile_collection$4d687194-7f5d-43a7-986b-b391a5c6b155",
